WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.660 --> 00:00:06.000
So, we move on to the final component, or rather aspect.

2
00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:07.780
It is security.

3
00:00:08.800 --> 00:00:12.100
What would I like to share on this front?

4
00:00:12.440 --> 00:00:18.000
First of all, the platform we work on itself – GitHub.

5
00:00:18.140 --> 00:00:24.800
It is unique, one could say – it is

6
00:00:24.800 --> 00:00:31.580
used by commercial organisations and by most of the world's

7
00:00:31.580 --> 00:00:33.520
open-source products.

8
00:00:35.260 --> 00:00:41.640
It is among the leaders in security among such platforms, so the platform itself is

9
00:00:41.640 --> 00:00:44.620
secure by default.

10
00:00:44.680 --> 00:00:51.020
Besides, the platform itself has many security tools and settings,

11
00:00:51.080 --> 00:00:54.260
and we have most of them turned on.

12
00:00:55.460 --> 00:01:01.280
Thanks to this, we get automatic detection of vulnerabilities

13
00:01:03.840 --> 00:01:10.240
and of various available security improvements, and it reaches us as recommendations.

14
00:01:10.440 --> 00:01:13.360
You can see, for example, "dependencies".

15
00:01:13.480 --> 00:01:20.400
This is exactly what came to us automatically from the built-in system:

16
00:01:20.460 --> 00:01:26.650
improvements for our portal and

17
00:01:26.650 --> 00:01:27.650
for automation.

18
00:01:29.650 --> 00:01:36.030
The second aspect is the security of access itself

19
00:01:36.030 --> 00:01:42.130
to protocol recordings for the general public.

20
00:01:44.500 --> 00:01:48.260
What do we have? Here we have

21
00:01:51.300 --> 00:01:56.120
metadata for recordings, including protocol ones.

22
00:01:59.820 --> 00:02:06.140
Here we have transcripts, subtitles and

23
00:02:06.140 --> 00:02:07.160
metadata.

24
00:02:08.500 --> 00:02:14.860
And the metadata could hold, right here, and it did before we added

25
00:02:15.160 --> 00:02:18.560
the feature, a link to the video, on Vimeo.

26
00:02:18.700 --> 00:02:22.020
The Vimeo link – it is…

27
00:02:22.020 --> 00:02:28.580
If you know it, you can watch the video without any restrictions.

28
00:02:29.020 --> 00:02:31.840
So the protection rests on nobody knowing the link.

29
00:02:33.490 --> 00:02:37.730
So if we put that link here, any automated system,

30
00:02:37.850 --> 00:02:40.010
anyone simply coming in from the internet,

31
00:02:40.010 --> 00:02:46.450
because our project is public, could take this video, open it in a new

32
00:02:46.450 --> 00:02:53.290
tab and get access to a protocol video, which is probably not

33
00:02:53.290 --> 00:02:54.290
right.

34
00:02:55.150 --> 00:03:01.150
That is why we use an encoding system: you see this link

35
00:03:01.150 --> 00:03:04.750
in a form you cannot just open.

36
00:03:05.970 --> 00:03:08.550
Several algorithms are applied in sequence,

37
00:03:09.790 --> 00:03:16.340
which turn this link into something you cannot simply turn back

38
00:03:16.340 --> 00:03:21.640
into a link. Only by knowing the order of these transformations can you

39
00:03:21.640 --> 00:03:27.560
restore it. So neither an automated system nor someone who opens the

40
00:03:27.560 --> 00:03:32.580
repository will get the link to a protocol video.

41
00:03:33.820 --> 00:03:37.760
But there is a second aspect – our portal.

42
00:03:38.000 --> 00:03:44.620
In our portal, when we click "View translation" or "Review translation", we also get

43
00:03:44.620 --> 00:03:51.240
the ability to play the video. And all these algorithms

44
00:03:51.240 --> 00:03:58.000
for decoding this form into the real link run in this portal. And to

45
00:03:58.000 --> 00:04:03.380
protect against someone who simply found this portal and opened it, whether

46
00:04:03.380 --> 00:04:07.140
an automated system or just anyone on the internet,

47
00:04:08.480 --> 00:04:11.740
so that nobody can come in and watch this video,

48
00:04:12.810 --> 00:04:16.050
including protocol ones, we have password protection.

49
00:04:16.610 --> 00:04:21.630
Everyone who has used this portal knows that when we click this button,

50
00:04:21.630 --> 00:04:28.530
we are asked for a password. Once entered, it is saved in the user's

51
00:04:28.530 --> 00:04:33.630
browser and not asked for again, so it seems there is no password for

52
00:04:33.630 --> 00:04:35.010
someone who has entered it once.

53
00:04:36.020 --> 00:04:42.960
These are the security aspects we use in

54
00:04:42.960 --> 00:04:47.460
working with this source code.

55
00:04:49.160 --> 00:04:55.720
Any user in the world can send proposals for changes.

56
00:04:56.260 --> 00:05:03.260
But only those who

57
00:05:03.260 --> 00:05:07.390
are in our group can make such changes.

58
00:05:09.280 --> 00:05:15.540
Let's find this group, and I'll just show you now how

59
00:05:15.540 --> 00:05:19.630
a new user is added.

60
00:05:19.670 --> 00:05:21.450
We happen to have an example.

61
00:05:21.450 --> 00:05:22.670
Now

62
00:05:25.870 --> 00:05:28.990
let's find it: here we have

63
00:05:30.080 --> 00:05:35.980
"Settings", and for this

64
00:05:35.980 --> 00:05:39.280
repository there are the users who are allowed.

65
00:05:39.700 --> 00:05:46.520
Right now it is my account, Dmytro Shcherbyna, Iryna

66
00:05:46.520 --> 00:05:47.520
Fil,

67
00:05:48.160 --> 00:05:52.640
Dmytro Yefremenko did not manage to join in the time we had, he did not

68
00:05:52.640 --> 00:05:53.900
have the time.

69
00:05:55.600 --> 00:06:02.470
And we still need to add, let's find her now,

70
00:06:04.900 --> 00:06:07.460
Anastasia – there is her email.

71
00:06:08.620 --> 00:06:13.280
We add her and

72
00:06:19.520 --> 00:06:24.120
say that she has "Write" access.

73
00:06:27.090 --> 00:06:30.210
And there are different access levels – that's it.

74
00:06:30.230 --> 00:06:33.270
Now Anastasia will accept this invitation

75
00:06:34.340 --> 00:06:38.860
and will be able to make changes, including to the system.

76
00:06:40.710 --> 00:06:42.110
To propose them, of course,

77
00:06:43.150 --> 00:06:46.370
when needed, and also to accept those changes.

78
00:06:49.060 --> 00:06:52.860
About how to hand over changes, how to take them,

79
00:06:56.580 --> 00:07:01.880
take them on yourself, mark that you have taken them into work –

80
00:07:02.020 --> 00:07:04.100
that will be in the next videos.

81
00:07:04.220 --> 00:07:10.840
That was just about the security aspects of our project. Jai Shri Mataji!
